  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Mzuzu Wind and Battery Storage Feasibility Study, through Enterprise - United States Unknown</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant funds a feasibility study for Mzuzu WF Limited that will assess the viability of a 50-megawatt wind energy project and a 100 megawatt-hour battery energy storage system near the city of Mzuzu in the northern region of Malawi. It will be one of the country&apos;s first utility-scale wind energy generation facilities and will significantly augment the country&apos;s current generation capacity of 442 MW while helping stabilize the national energy grid and enhance resilience to climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
